      "showAdvanced": null,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "SDR to HDR",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Pick an 8-bit image or video in Read.\n2. SDR to HDR Universal turns it into scene-linear HDR (1.0 = 203 nits). Its learned mode uses the RUDRA model, downloaded on first run (about 5 MB; weights are licensed for non-commercial use, see the README).\n3. The Viewer shows the result through ACES 2.0; a normal preview shows values above 1.0 as white.\n4. Write saves a 32-bit float EXR. Set output_path and filename to taste.\n\nThe report output says whether the learned recovery ran."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
